  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Afro-Curaçaoan song and dance in which a lead singer improvises topical, often critical verses answered by a chorus, over a single tambú drum, the chapi (a hoe blade struck with a metal rod) and hand-clapping. Long restricted by colonial law and condemned by the Catholic church, it is especially sung in the weeks before the New Year and is now a pillar of Curaçaoan heritage; the bell card stands in for the chapi.",
